* <Natural Source Header
* -------------------------------------------------------------------- *
* RMSTX--N Handle Subtasks on Unix Systems
*
* Functions:
* ----------
*
* SUBMIT/START
* ------------
* Start a Unix task.
* STX-START-SCRIPT     - Script/program name
* STX-LOGFILE          - File for script output
* STX-TASK-NUMBER      - Number of a monitor task to be started
*
* If a printer task is already active, it will be posted, not started.
*
* STATUS
* ------
* Information if a task is running
* STX-TASK-NAME        - Task name according to NRM-SUBTASK-INFO
*                        (fully or not fully qualified)
*
* LIST
* ------
* List tasks sequentially and return their status
* STX-TASK-NAME        - Task name according to NRM-SUBTASK-INFO
*                        (fully or not fully qualified)
*
* KILL
* ----
* Kill a task
* STX-TASK-NAME        - Task name according to NRM-SUBTASK-INFO
*
*
* Status values in STX-TASK-STATUS
*  0: Task is running
*  1: Task is stopped
*  2: Status unknown
*
*
* Codes of NPR Unix function 'STATUS' and resulting STX-TASK-STATUS
*
* xsetggr 2011-07-04 NoMALL-1002 corrected status code handling
* codes 6-12 (except 8) are assume as unknown and after pause status of
* task checked again. If remains the same - set 1 (task stopped).
*
*
*  NPR Status Value        STX-TASK-STATUS
*  ------------------------- ------------
*  0: UNKNOWN                     2
*  1: NOT FOUND                   1
*  2: SLEEPING                    0
*  3: WAITING                     0
*  4: RUNNING                     0
*  5: IN INTERMEDIATE STATE       0
*  6: TERMINATED                  2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 was 1
*  7: STOPPED                     2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 was 1
*  8: GROWING                     2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 was 0
*  9: IN UNKNOWN STATE            2
* 10: FINISHED                    2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 in
* 11: WINDOWS SERVICE PAUSED      2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 in
* 12: ZOMBIE PROCESS              2    /* xsetggr NOMALL-1002 in
*
*
* Message codes of a script, filled with function STATUS:
*  STX-MESSAGE-CODE - Return code of the script in question
*  STX-MESSAGE      - Text for abended script
*
* The started bash script requires the following handling:
* 1. After the main command save the return code (i.e batch Natural)
*    exitcode=$?
* 2. Enter the following last 2 lines:
*    set -x
*    exit $exitcode
*
* Note: Caller has to do an END TRANSACTION, this module must not do it
*
* -------------------------------------------------------------------- *
*
* MAINTENANCE:
* ------------
* User ID yyyy-mm-dd Mark      Comment
* fhi     2005-06-27 P266530   Created
* fhi     2005-09-28 P270015   Task does not start
* fhi     2005-10-14 P(266530) Recompiled, XXUX---P changed.
* fhi     2007-03-13 FHI212    Recompiled, XXUX---P changed.
* fhi     2007-03-26 FHI212    XXUX---n rewritten
* fhi     2008-07-04 P304914   Error number not returned.
* fhi     2010-08-11 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking for Unix           STEM
* fhi     2010-08-18 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking for Unix           STEM
* fhi     2010-08-20 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking, rewritten, no tagsSTEM
* fhi     2010-08-23 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking, no tags           STEM
* fhi     2010-09-28 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking, no tags           STEM
* fhi     2010-09-28 NOMALL-853 Monitor Multitasking, no tags           STEM
* fhi     2010-11-05 NOMALL-97  Extend tracing, no tags
* fhi     2011-01-03 NOMALL-853 Avoid deadlock (NAT3009, subcode 6)     STEM
*                               No tags.                                STEM
* fhi     2011-02-01 NOMALL-948 Avoid destroyed buffer pool             STEM
* fhi     2011-02-01 NOMALL-922 Reuse printer tasks                     STEM
* fhi     2011-02-07 NOMALL-929 Avoid 3009 and dead locks (Subcode 6)   STEM
*                               No tags for this.
* fhi     2011-03-23 NOMALL-947 Handle Status call with PID 0           STEM
* fhi     2011-05-26 NOMALL-1000 Avoid NAT1314 in 3030                  STEM
* xsetggr 2011-07-04 NOMALL-1002 handle corrections of NPROS-35
* xsetggr 2011-07-06 NOMALL-1002 correct retry time
* fhi     2012-04-04 NOMALL-1135 Status interpretation changed for AIX
*                                Can be backouted after solution of
*                                iTrac NPROS-53 or with NPR Unix
*                                prerequitsite NPR 2.1.4.11 or higher
* fhi     2012-04-10 NOMALL-1135 Backouted, old version kept in NOM33OLD
*                                No tags entered for backout.
